  "situation": "The Secretary of State must decide whether Taiwan and Korea fall within the US defensive perimeter. US policymakers were focused on Europe, and the administration faced limits on available resources and pressure to concentrate commitments on defensible points of clear value. Military views supported a limited perimeter, while the prospect of Soviet involvement on Taiwan raised concern about sea lanes. The administration had disengaged from the Chinese civil war, and US forces had withdrawn from Korea. The decision concerns the scope of a US defense commitment amid competing assessments of strategic value and risk.",
